<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:58:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Why have US-Ukraine relations soured ahead of the midterms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1f87e16a2d8c7d25ee57479241af8499bc618a32cd83ce5ce5e8b15078a5a9b</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T17:54:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-why-have-us-ukraine-relations-soured-ahead-of-the-midterms--b38db7502a5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-why-have-us-ukraine-relations-soured-ahead-of-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said he felt “betrayed” on Wednesday after access was seemingly restricted to US intelligence and Space X satellite services, raising new questions about US commitment to Ukraine. With Trump under pressure over rising fuel prices, is the White House hoping criticism of Kyiv can help shift the blame?</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Election delay 'a terrible disappointment', Palestinian activist Samer Sinijlawi says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:809aeb325253672d047e2d18ac543c9eb60c13132f184dc53e3873ca9b679579</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:17:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261015-election-delay-a-terrible-disappointment-palestinian-activist-samer-sinijlawi-says--df16dcb36eae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261015-election-delay-a-terrible-disappointment-palestinian-activist-samer-sinijlawi-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Palestinian activist Samer Sinijlawi called the postponement of the first legislative elections in 20 years to September 2027 "a terrible disappointment" for a generation that has never had a chance to vote. He also dismissed the citing of Israeli restrictions as an excuse, pointing instead to a "rejection" of change among ageing Palestinian leaders.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>'We're done': Ukraine resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries as 'only leverage' for peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20a5fe3623537efcb9bda9080beea2069e07289aca7e1cfb2a08f30be5393718</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:14:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-tal--b4d9641c071b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-talks-1" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. As Zelensky declares Ukraine "done" with Trump's self-declared energy ceasefire and resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries, Zalmayev warns: "When you talk about the energy ceasefire, it presupposes two to be able to tango and to dance this dance." He challenges the legitimacy of Trump's unilateral announcement, made without agreement between Moscow and Kyiv, as Russia continues attacking Ukraine's energy infrastructure. Yet he cautions that Zelensky may need tactical restraint to preserve vital US support. Zalmayev also examines Western sanctions, frozen Russian assets, and Washington's pursuit of economic normalization with Moscow without meaningful Russian concessions.</summary></entry><entry><title>India’s Cockroach movement: Protesters bypass internet blackout with Bluetooth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a566aaa94dd56bce13f0e952c1324107034741bcdd11514e0da2e2857a57719e</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T15:29:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-india-s-cockroach-movement-protesters-bypass-internet-blackout-with-bluetooth--dfbcc10c75b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-india-s-cockroach-movement-protesters-bypass-internet-blackout-with-bluetooth" /><summary type="html">🇮🇳 On October 10, New Delhi faced a near-lockdown situation following a call for protests by Gen Z-led Cockroach Janta Party. Authorities imposed a 24-hour internet blackout, but protesters found ways around it.</summary></entry><entry><title>2026 Midterms: Georgia's Ossof-Collins showdown lies at the heart of the battle for US Senate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9aba4145a7cff414f2f5fd05e234ce969a8f17f8b078b18848ffac1e909d161d</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T15:14:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-2026-midterms-georgia-s-ossof-collins-showdown-lies-at-the-heart-of-the-battle-for-us-senat--052a42259b79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-2026-midterms-georgia-s-ossof-collins-showdown-lies-at-the-heart-of-the-battle-for-us-senate" /><summary type="html">In Georgia, Democrat Jon Ossoff’s seat is one of the key contests in the US mid-term elections on 3 November. In this state, which was won by Donald Trump in 2024, the incumbent senator is facing Republican Mike Collins. Our reporter Leela Jacinto visited Manuel’s Tavern, a historic bar in Atlanta that has been frequented for decades by Democratic politicians. There, patrons watched the debate between the two candidates.</summary></entry><entry><title>France charges teen shooter citing revenge for bullying in school</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40b5a7a35b633c80bdd278810c5de3ce9ddb0337c2e09b83a6184b6f31eb077b</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T15:06:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-france-charges-teen-shooter-citing-revenge-for-bullying-in-school--4c40d5dd17a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-france-charges-teen-shooter-citing-revenge-for-bullying-in-school" /><summary type="html">A 14-year-old charged with attempted murder in France after wounding a principal and a teacher in a school shooting this week said he acted out of revenge for bullying, prosecutors have said. The incident, at a middle school for 11- to 15-years-olds, is not thought to have any link with ongoing high school protests nationwide to demand better learning conditions.</summary></entry><entry><title>US consumer inflation hotter than expected as midterms loom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e924daf89c35b97068530e98a248c11b6709d1b98e3667ba662dadb8f4929c09</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T15:05:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-us-consumer-inflation-hotter-than-expected-as-midterms-loom--723e95592f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-us-consumer-inflation-hotter-than-expected-as-midterms-loom" /><summary type="html">US consumer inflation was hotter than anticipated in September, government data showed Wednesday, as Washington's continued war with Tehran pushed energy costs higher, deepening strains on American households ahead of next month's midterm elections. The uptick underscores voter worries over high costs of living, and comes as President Donald Trump is campaigning in US states to shore up support for his Republican Party as it tries to retain control of Congress.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel ex-security chief sues Netanyahu over October 7 claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95077589f54cb71e5dc6cb5b3c2ffaa7b20b89f95c754b873fe8129d46c91b11</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T15:04:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-israel-ex-security-chief-sues-netanyahu-over-october-7-claims--e3d017f1d95d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-israel-ex-security-chief-sues-netanyahu-over-october-7-claims" /><summary type="html">The former head of Israel's Shin Bet domestic security agency on Wednesday sued Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu for defamation weeks before elections in a row over responsibility for Hamas's October 7, 2023 attack. Netanyahu, who polls show in a tight race to stay in power in the October 27 election, has been hammered by the opposition for failing to prevent the attack, the deadliest day in Israeli history. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Police and protesters face off in Albania on third day of anti-govt demonstrations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca5919749a20ddf2709bcc0eec05fe5cc45ea028c5d7d64c1969a6505053dac7</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T15:02:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-police-and-protesters-face-off-in-albania-on-third-day-of-anti-govt-demonstrations--9e582ef14589.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-police-and-protesters-face-off-in-albania-on-third-day-of-anti-govt-demonstrations" /><summary type="html">Demonstrators and riot police clashed in Albania's capital on Thursday in a third straight day of violence triggered by student protests calling for better university conditions and Prime Minister Edi Rama's resignation. Originally sparked by a luxury tourism project linked to US President Donald Trump's family in the country's south, the demonstrations have occasionally flared into violence amid ongoing calls for Rama's resignation. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Former US generals push to stop 'barbaric' firing squad execution livestream</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62e4728a76a0bb904ea7af1578ec8933a3cab6fcc93e2aeec9df4e0d95c8b844</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T15:01:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-former-us-generals-push-to-stop-barbaric-firing-squad-execution-livestream--a53d4b3355cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-former-us-generals-push-to-stop-barbaric-firing-squad-execution-livestream" /><summary type="html">A group of 72 retired US generals, admirals, and other high-ranking military officers have urged authorities to cancel plans to livestream the firing squad execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hassan – bringing legal arguments and the dangerous consequences such a broadcast would have. A government execution has never been broadcast or livestreamed, according to death penalty experts, and the US military ​has not executed anyone by firing squad since 1945.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine struggles with Starlink and US satellite data as missiles hit Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54fd7748cb0c142d815b32a2e197c0bc366a4889f4a06219cb6668904f2d9a88</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:59:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-ukraine-struggles-with-starlink-and-us-satellite-data-as-missiles-hit-kyiv--e29a8f7958ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-ukraine-struggles-with-starlink-and-us-satellite-data-as-missiles-hit-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Ukraine on Wednesday accused the United States of helping Russia by failing to warn it of incoming missile strikes and hobbling Kyiv's military response through changes to the Starlink system it uses on the battlefield. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky called on US tech billionaire Elon Musk to restore Starlink, which Kyiv says has been slowed down.</summary></entry><entry><title>Fort Hood shooter’s firing squad execution will not be livestreamed, Trump says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2af245b499ce4af3f781954e78f9e81091f8e8f140c488024ebc44248286efd</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:58:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-fort-hood-shooter-s-firing-squad-execution-will-not-be-livestreamed-trump-says--e314adab8cb1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-fort-hood-shooter-s-firing-squad-execution-will-not-be-livestreamed-trump-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Thursday that he was cancelling plans to livestream the firing squad execution of a convicted military base shooter – a project that had sparked outrage in the United States. Nidal Hasan is scheduled to be executed on December 3 at Fort Hood in Texas, where he killed 13 people in 2009.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Pink October in France: A toxic debate?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa0d214b7529a832ba09d2e70e657a146c8ac9a72922eded0004cab578803a23</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:45:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261015-pink-october-in-france-a-toxic-debate--2bad24532f08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261015-pink-october-in-france-a-toxic-debate" /><summary type="html">Pink October – the French version of Breast Cancer Awareness Month – is at the centre of a political storm here in France, after one MP said she refused to wear a pink ribbon, calling the month "utterly cynical". We dive into her reasoning, discuss the history of Breast Cancer Awareness Month, and learn how to look out for "pinkwashing".</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Haiti: Capoeira classes aim to promote peace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21b4210b62a36837f751b836daeedb6b7d653286fa4f96465ad55319d331fbbf</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:25:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261015-haiti-capoeira-classes-promote-peace--3eb12a28ea75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261015-haiti-capoeira-classes-promote-peace" /><summary type="html">An association in Haiti is organising capoeira classes – an Afro-Brazilian martial art – in an attempt to reduce community violence and promote social reintegration. The Observers team spoke to its founder, Rodney Jean Marc, who said their doors are open to everyone, “even children in armed gangs”. The initiative takes place as the country's security situation has worsened in recent years.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>War escalates between Houthis and Riyadh: How did we get here?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f22130d01f5a45a42b995b56d78b9d37afb1ad14e013a2bdea83b84cee572f7</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:16:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261015-war-escalates-between-houthis-and-riyadh-how-did-we-get-here--f6da2e88a028.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261015-war-escalates-between-houthis-and-riyadh-how-did-we-get-here" /><summary type="html">To discuss the ongoing conflict between the Houthi rebels and the Saudi-backed coalition, we speak to Jules Grange Gastinel, a researcher at France's CNRS research body specialising in the Houthi movement. He tells us why the conflict has escalated and what the Houthis want.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>NATO to address drone attacks in the Black Sea after seven missing off Romania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf17a39aa480201c93a579a3f82da3675512ceabc199fe4e9469071d035938c8</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:35:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks--d31e01c8ba8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks" /><summary type="html">NATO will put drone strikes in the Black Sea on its agenda at a meeting next week, officials said Thursday, following two new attacks and the disappearance of seven people. Incidents involving civilian vessels in the Black Sea have been on the rise off the coasts of Bulgaria and Romania in a suspected spillover from Russia’s war in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French crypto unicorn Ledger warns of AI security risks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52bc817a4d6369af2c8c7832ea22059af9a1b3aa973594982a30532cf300cd94</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:58:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:31:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261015-french-crypto-unicorn-ledger-warns-of-ai-security-risks--cf5135c238b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261015-french-crypto-unicorn-ledger-warns-of-ai-security-risks" /><summary type="html">Artificial intelligence is "changing the security landscape". That's according to Ledger, a French unicorn of cryptocurrency that's seeking a bigger role in digital security. Chief Technology Officer Charles Guillemet says: "Finding vulnerabilities and exploiting them costs almost nothing. So this is the new challenge that we have, as the security industry in general – how can we raise the bar for security so it becomes so difficult to break systems? And I think hardware is part of the equation."</summary><category term="People &amp; Profit" /></entry><entry><title>‘Amazing progress’ in lung cancer: Immunotherapy extends survival as mRNA vaccines offer hope</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6972ed320a8b197b7f2ed319c9dd3c2e02bc80a220472220a0dec449bc97da8</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:58:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:22:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261015-amazing-progress-in-lung-cancer-immunotherapy-extends-survival-as-mrna-vaccines-offer-hope--3413e95d0ebc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261015-amazing-progress-in-lung-cancer-immunotherapy-extends-survival-as-mrna-vaccines-offer-hope" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Siow-Ming Lee, Professor of Medical Oncology at the University College London and a specialist in lung cancer. “Lung cancer is not one cancer. There are many different types of lung cancer,” explains Lee. For decades, lung cancer has been closely associated with smoking, late diagnosis and poor survival prospects. Yet there is a broader revolution in cancer brewing: Medicine advances in molecular oncology, minimally invasive surgery and immunotherapy are fundamentally transforming both the understanding and treatment of the disease, including among patients who have never smoked.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>From Lupin's return to a bloody culinary apocalypse: The TV shows to watch this month</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1fb194bab06f7692d3ed0cd32be2eb4e19bc7f0ab75e75348d06c4ab7fb4374</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:58:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:08:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261015-from-lupin-s-return-to-a-bloody-culinary-apocalypse-the-tv-shows-to-watch-this-month--b46f43a389d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261015-from-lupin-s-return-to-a-bloody-culinary-apocalypse-the-tv-shows-to-watch-this-month" /><summary type="html">TV critic Dheepthika Laurent takes us through this month's TV highlights, starting with the long-awaited return of "Lupin", Netflix's most-watched French series. Omar Sy is back as the gentleman thief, but this time someone appears to be stealing in his name. Can France's favourite master of disguise clear his name?</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Elon Musk and Donald Trump: What their growing ties mean for Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a99f915b3647ae9d2e9bca2697e2bb3bece6a13054d8c1faa0177aea14a8b0a</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:56:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T12:39:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-elon-musk-and-donald-trump-what-their-growing-ties-mean-for-ukraine--8794b197d954.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-elon-musk-and-donald-trump-what-their-growing-ties-mean-for-ukraine" /><summary type="html">The recent disruption of SpaceX’s Starlink satellite internet service in Ukraine comes as Washington steps up pressure on Kyiv to halt its strikes on Russian oil refineries. The system plays a key role in Ukraine’s long-range drone operations, raising questions about the implications of the disruption and Elon Musk’s increasingly close ties with Donald Trump.</summary></entry><entry><title>Chad’s ICC exit plans raise concerns over Sudan war crimes probes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b009f22b01a1bece34236373a729670d70bce1c2d94af8af4b06c46491d087ee</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:56:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T12:36:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-chad-s-icc-exit-plans-raise-concerns-over-sudan-war-crimes-probes--c2ff38d9bb00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-chad-s-icc-exit-plans-raise-concerns-over-sudan-war-crimes-probes" /><summary type="html">Last July, Chad announced plans to withdraw from the International Criminal Court, accusing it of inefficiency and of disproportionately targeting African nations. The decision could complicate future investigations into alleged war crimes linked to the conflict in neighbouring Sudan, particularly as ICC investigators engage with Sudanese refugees sheltering in eastern Chad. Despite the political headwinds, humanitarian organisations remain on the ground, supporting those displaced by the crisis, as FRANCE 24’s Harold Girard reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's Zelensky defies Trump with Russian refinery strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79f8239d3bb0509412362a65b746b5fd3f8e6f1b6054fb8a94d87307aab5b432</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:56:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T12:34:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-ukraine-s-zelensky-defies-trump-with-russian-refinery-strikes--381ed3df5d09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-ukraine-s-zelensky-defies-trump-with-russian-refinery-strikes" /><summary type="html">Ukraine will no longer abide by US President Donald Trump's demands not to strike Russian oil refineries, President Volodymyr Zelensky said in remarks published Thursday, amid deepening tensions between the two leaders over a US-Russia diesel agreement. Relations between Kyiv and Washington have soured since last week, when Trump eased sanctions on Russia in exchange for Moscow releasing large amounts of diesel onto global markets. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Outcry over US plans to livestream firing squad execution of Fort Hood shooter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20b943df08c68969da4fc98006cc6f2575a11cd74e10179e1fd607cf6e96ec9b</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:56:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T12:33:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-outcry-over-us-plans-to-livestream-firing-squad-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter--fdcc7532b393.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-outcry-over-us-plans-to-livestream-firing-squad-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter" /><summary type="html">US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth last week announced plans to livestream the firing squad execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hasan, triggering a backlash among Republicans in Congress, religious leaders and international observers. The event would be extraordinary, even for a country that has long employed capital punishment. A government execution has never been broadcast or livestreamed, according to death penalty experts, and the US military ​has not executed anyone by firing squad since 1945. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Student protests spread in Albania as demonstrators call for PM resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed3df4cd2d367bb463e84e3a4ed3f249ab04b0d7fec1a589a637423cc166d290</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:58:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T12:27:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-student-protests-escalate-in-albania-as-demonstrators-call-for-pm-resignation--ceb6c228c280.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-student-protests-escalate-in-albania-as-demonstrators-call-for-pm-resignation" /><summary type="html">Clashes broke out between demonstrators and police for the third consecutive day on Thursday in Albania, with Prime Minister Edi Rama condemning the “chaos” that caused damage to government buildings. Thousands of protesters are calling for Rama's resignation and better studying conditions for Albanian students.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
